{"book":6,"chapter":4,"context":{"chapter":4,"title":"Twelve Stones of Memory","summary":"Twelve men, one from each tribe, carry stones from the riverbed to Gilgal as a memorial, and Joshua sets up another twelve in the river. When the priests step out, the Jordan returns to its banks.","background":"Israel crossed on the tenth day of the first month (v. 19), the day Passover lambs were chosen (Exodus 12:3), forty years after the Exodus. Gilgal, near Jericho, became Israel's base camp. About forty thousand armed men from the eastern tribes crossed first, keeping their promise to Moses (vv. 12–13).","customs":[{"term":"Memorial stones","verses":"4:6-7","note":"A pile of stones served as a lasting marker of what had happened in a place. When children asked what the stones meant, parents would tell the story."}],"watchFor":["A child's question again opens the door to the story (vv. 6, 21), as in Deuteronomy 6:20.","God 'magnified Joshua' as he had promised (v. 14; 3:7).","The goal: that all peoples know God's power and Israel fear him (v. 24)."],"connections":["Exodus 12:3","Deuteronomy 6:20-21","1 Samuel 7:12"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["וַיְהִי","vayhi","H1961","Hc/Vqw3ms","and it was"],["כַּאֲשֶׁר","ka'asher-","H834","HR/Tr","just when"],["תַּמּוּ","tamu","H8552","HVqp3cp","they had finished"],["כָל","khol-","H3605","HNcmsc","all"],["הַגּוֹי","hagoy","H1471","HTd/Ncmsa","the nation"],["לַעֲבוֹר","la'avor","H5674","HR/Vqcc","to pass over"],["אֶת","'et-","H853","HTo","<obj.>"],["הַיַּרְדֵּן","haiyarden","H3383","HTd/Npl","the Jordan"],["וַיֹּאמֶר","vaiyomer","H559","Hc/Vqw3ms","and he said"],["יְהוָה","yahweh","H3068","HNpt","Yahweh"],["אֶל","'el-","H413","HR","to"],["יְהוֹשֻׁעַ","yehoshua'","H3091","HNpm","Joshua"],["לֵאמֹר","lemor","H559","HR/Vqcc","<to> saying"]],"x":[[5027002,5027002,8],[6003017,6003017,3]],"xn":2},"2":{"w":[["קְחוּ","kechu","H3947","HVqv2mp","take"],["לָכֶם","lakhem","H9036","HRd/Sp2mp","for <the> yourselves"],["מִן","min-","H4480","HR","from"],["הָע